## When to load the reference files

This SKILL.md covers the 20% you'll need 80% of the time. When the user's request touches specific subsystems, **load the appropriate reference file** from the same directory before answering:

- **`REFERENCE.md`** — Complete module inventory (196 files, categorized). Load when the user asks "where does X live" or "what does `forge_Y` do".
- **`BACKENDS.md`** — LLM backends, provider cascades, model map, NPU cascade details. Load for routing/performance questions.
- **`ARCHITECTURE.md`** — Engrid v3 layers, Rings, TruthState, MeshMemory, sovereign membrane. Load for data-flow or integrity questions.
- **`CLAWHUB.md`** — Skill marketplace, API endpoints, SkillGuardian review, installed catalog. Load for `@skill` or skill-related questions.
- **`CTF.md`** — Exegol toolbox, forge_ctf_agent pipeline, pwn/reverse/web helpers. Load for CTF or offensive-security work.
- **`RECON.md`** — Recon silo, MsfRpcClient, ChainEngine live/sandbox, network_profiler. Load for network recon / pentest pipeline questions.
- **`SECURITY.md`** — NoiseGuardian, TrustBroker, forge_integrity, forge_prompt_guard, env_crypt. Load for security/anonymization questions.

Use `view` tool on the relevant file before producing a substantive answer. The cost is low; the accuracy gain is significant.

